# OpenEVV sound map: Pennsylvania Dutch (Lehigh) (eSpeak NG voice gmw/pdc-x-lehigh), spoken by openevv's German module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template dedx
style standard
vowels i I e E a A u U o O y Y oe OE @ aj aw oj a~ E~ o~ oe~ E: R
glides r l j w
schwa @
secondary 2

# the melody: peak; a question that wants yes or no: risefall
accent f0=own range=90 shape=0 accent=26 accent2=12 unstressed=-6 decl=8 declmax=30 fs=-18 fw=-12 fc=10 fe=-12 fq=34 qreg=8 span=2 qfall=50 stop=1

# the words a question is asked with, which is not the question that wants yes or no
whwords first wer was wu wann wie ferwas weller wieviel

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says J d Z
says P p f
says T t s

